From: Brian 'redbeard' Harrington <redbeard@dead-city.org>
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Platform/Spacemit/K3: Cpu.asl _LPI (WFI + CPU_NR) + \_SB platform _OSC (Task 9)

Platform/Spacemit/K3: Cpu.asl _LPI (WFI + CPU_NR) + \_SB platform _OSC (Task 9)

_LPI on every ACPI0007 processor device, structured for the kernel's
index-0 semantics (__CPU_PM_CPU_IDLE_ENTER treats index 0 specially:
cpu_do_idle(), NO SBI suspend entry - a state at index 0 never
suspends):

- State 0 "WFI": explicit shallow state, FFH address 0, timer runs.
  Occupies the index-0 special path so usage counts are honest.
- State 1 "CPU_NR": FFH address (1<<60)|0x90000000 =
  0x1000000090000000, min-residency 950us, wake 500us, Flags ENABLED
  (bit 0 - flatten_lpi_states skips states without it), ArchFlags
  bit 0 (local timer stops, per the DT idle-state's
  local-timer-stop). The RISC-V FFH encoding keeps bits[59:32]
  reserved zero - the param lives in the LOW 32 bits (the CPPC FFH
  convention in this file).

CLUSTER_NR deliberately DEFERRED: cluster qualification requires
validating the wake mechanism (tick broadcast under timer-stop, M2
coordination with ESOS), not just boot success.

Kernel companion note: 6.12 RISC-V has no
arch_get_idle_state_flags override (weak default returns 0; only
ARM64 maps CPUIDLE_CORE_CTXT to CPUIDLE_FLAG_TIMER_STOP) - a one-
line kernel override mapping ArchFlags bit 0 is required for the
timer-stop flag to take effect on this kernel. The AML is correct
and forward-compatible with the upstream mapping.

\_SB platform-wide _OSC (UUID 0811B06E-...) confirming PCLPI (0x80)
ONLY: acpi_processor_get_lpi_info() gates _LPI parsing on
osc_pc_lpi_support_confirmed, set exclusively by this handshake
(root cause of the original silent no-cpuidle failure; proven live:
'platform _OSC: OS control mask [00000080]'). The buffer is 2
DWORDs (u32 capbuf[2]: Query/Status, Support - NO Control DWORD).
Revision != 1 returns _OSC_REVISION_ERROR (0x08); unknown UUIDs
return _OSC_UNRECOGNIZED_UUID (0x04, not the query bit). PR3/S3,
GED, hotplug-OST not confirmed. (PCI0's _OSC keeps CDW3:
pci_root.c passes capbuf[5].)

Latencies are vendor DT values - measure before freezing.

Validation: full RELEASE build; built DSDT decompiles 8x (WFI,
CPU_NR) with Flags=One, ArchFlags=One on CPU_NR, correct FFH
addresses, zero CLUSTER_NR, and the \\_SB _OSC with revision/UUID
error paths. Hardware gates closed live so far: _OSC presence,
buffer contract. Encoding/flags/index fixes verified in AML only.
